ution to congenital heart defects. <source>Development.</source> <volume>128</volume>:<fpage>1531</fpage>&#x02013;1538.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11290292</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib15"><citation citation-type="journal">Frid, M.G., V.A. Kale, and K.R. Stenmark. <year>2002</year>. Mature vascular endothelium can give rise to smooth muscle cells via endothelial-mesenchymal transdifferentiation: in vitro analysis. <source>Circ. Res.</source> <volume>90</volume>:<fpage>1189</fpage>&#x02013;1196.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12065322</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib16"><citation citation-type="journal">Goumans, M.J., G. Valdimarsdottir, S. Itoh, A. Rosendahl, P. Sideras, and P. ten Dijke. <year>2002</year>. Balancing the activation state of the endothelium via two distinct TGF-beta type I receptors. <source>EMBO J.</source> <volume>21</volume>:<fpage>1743</fpage>&#x02013;1753.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11927558</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib17"><citation citation-type="journal">Gumbiner, B.M. <year>1995</year>. Signal transduction by &#x003b2;-catenin. <source>Curr. Opin. Cell Biol.</source> <volume>7</volume>:<fpage>634</fpage>&#x02013;640.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8573337</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib18"><citation citation-type="journal">Hurlstone, A., and H. Clevers. <year>2002</year>. T-cell factors: turn-ons and turn-offs. <source>EMBO J.</source> <volume>21</volume>:<fpage>2303</fpage>&#x02013;2311.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12006483</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib19"><citation citation-type="journal">Hurlstone, A.F., A.P. Haramis, E. Wienholds, H. Begthel, J. Korving, F. Van Eeden, E. Cuppen, D. Zivkovic, R.H. Plasterk, and H. Clevers. <year>2003</year>. The Wnt/beta-catenin pathway regulates cardiac valve formation. <source>Nature.</source> <volume>425</volume>:<fpage>633</fpage>&#x02013;637.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14534590</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib20"><citation citation-type="journal">Itoh, S., F. Itoh, M.J. Goumans, and P. Ten Dijke. <year>2000</year>. Signaling of transforming growth factor-beta family members through Smad proteins. <source>Eur. J. Biochem.</source> <volume>267</volume>:<fpage>6954</fpage>&#x02013;6967.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11106403</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib21"><citation citation-type="journal">Iurlaro, M., M. Scatena, W.H. Zhu, E. Fogel, S.L. Wieting, and R.F. Nicosia. <year>2003</year>. Rat aorta-derived mural precursor cells express the Tie2 receptor and respond directly to stimulation by angiopoietins. <source>J. Cell Sci.</source> <volume>116</volume>:<fpage>3635</fpage>&#x02013;3643.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12876214</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib22"><citation citation-type="journal">Iwamoto, R., S. Yamazaki, M. Asakura, S. Takashima, H. Hasuwa, K. Miyado, S. Adachi, M. Kitakaze, K. Hashimoto, G. Raab, et al. <year>2003</year>. Heparin-binding EGF-like growth factor and ErbB signaling is essential for heart function. <source>Proc. Natl. Acad. Sci. USA.</source> <volume>100</volume>:<fpage>3221</fpage>&#x02013;3226.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12621152</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib23"><citation citation-type="journal">Kim, R.Y., E.J. Robertson, and M.J. Solloway. <year>2001</year>. Bmp6 and Bmp7 are required for cushion formation and septation in the developing mouse heart. <source>Dev. Biol.</source> <volume>235</volume>:<fpage>449</fpage>&#x02013;466.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11437450</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib24"><citation citation-type="journal">Kisanuki, Y.Y., R.E. Hammer, J. Miyazaki, S.C. Williams, J.A. Richardson, and M. Yanagisawa. <year>2001</year>. Tie2-Cre transgenic mice: a new model for endothelial cell-lineage analysis in vivo. <source>Dev. Biol.</source> <volume>230</volume>:<fpage>230</fpage>&#x02013;242.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11161575</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib25"><citation citation-type="journal">Labbe, E., A. Letamendia, and L. Attisano. <year>2000</year>. Association of Smads with lymphoid enhancer binding factor 1/T cell-specific factor mediates cooperative signaling by the transforming growth factor-beta and wnt pathways. <source>Proc. Natl. Acad. Sci. USA.</source> <volume>97</volume>:<fpage>8358</fpage>&#x02013;8363.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10890911</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib26"><citation citation-type="journal">Lampugnani, M.G., A. Zanetti, F. Breviario, G. Balconi, F. Orsenigo, M. Corada, R. Spagnuolo, M. Betson, V. Braga, and E. Dejana. <year>2002</year>. VE-cadherin regulates endothelial actin activating Rac and increasing membrane association of Tiam. <source>Mol. Biol. Cell.</source> <volume>13</volume>:<fpage>1175</fpage>&#x02013;1189.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11950930</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib27"><citation citation-type="journal">Liebner, S., A. Fischmann, G. Rascher, F. Duffner, E.H. Grote, H. Kalbacher, and H. Wolburg. <year>2000</year>. Claudin-1 and claudin-5 expression and tight junction morphology are altered in blood vessels of human glioblastoma multiforme. <source>Acta Neuropathol. (Berl.).</source> <volume>100</volume>:<fpage>323</fpage>&#x02013;331.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10965803</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib28"><citation citation-type="journal">Lu, C., G. Schwartzbauer, M.A. Sperling, S.U. Devaskar, S. Thamotharan, P.D. Robbins, C.F. McTiernan, J.L. Liu, J. Jiang, S.J. Frank, and R.K. Menon. <year>2001</year>. Demonstration of direct effects of growth hormone on neonatal cardiomyocytes. <source>J. Biol. Chem.</source> <volume>276</volume>:<fpage>22892</fpage>&#x02013;22900.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11303022</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib29"><citation citation-type="journal">Maretto, S., M. Cordenonsi, S. Dupont, P. Braghetta, V. Broccoli, A.B. Hassan, D. Volpin, G.M. Bressan, and S. Piccolo. <year>2003</year>. Mapping Wnt/beta-catenin signaling during mouse development and in colorectal tumors. <source>Proc. Natl. Acad. Sci. USA.</source> <volume>100</volume>:<fpage